WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.786
Mary looked at the key for quite a long time.

2
00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:08.662
She turned it over in her hand, thinking.

3
00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:14.735
If this were the key to the secret garden, all she had to do now was find the door!

4
00:00:14.736 --> 00:00:19.538
She liked the idea of going into the garden and playing there by herself.

5
00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:22.897
No one would even know she was there.

6
00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:29.151
She put the key in her pocket, and strolled up and down her favorite path outside the walled gardens.

7
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:35.336
Nobody but Mary ever seemed to go there, so she could walk slowly and look at the wall closely.

8
00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:40.526
But no matter how carefully she looked, she could see nothing but ivy.

9
00:00:40.527 --> 00:00:44.031
She was very disappointed.

10
00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:50.271
"It seems so silly," she said, "to be near that garden and not be able to get in!"

11
00:00:50.272 --> 00:00:54.149
She decided that she would always carry the key with her.

12
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.780
That way, if she ever found the hidden door, she would be ready.

13
00:00:58.781 --> 00:01:05.877
The next morning when Mary woke up, Martha was back at work and full of stories about her day off.

14
00:01:05.878 --> 00:01:11.669
She left the room for a moment and came back, holding something under her apron.

15
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.851
"I've brought you a present!" she said with a grin.

16
00:01:15.852 --> 00:01:24.911
"A present!" Mary wondered how someone from a cottage filled with so many hungry people could give anyone a present.

17
00:01:24.912 --> 00:01:28.939
"A man was driving across the moor selling things.

18
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.253
He stopped his cart at our door, and Mother bought you a skipping rope with some of my wages."

19
00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:40.396
Martha brought the rope out from underneath her apron and held it out proudly.

20
00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:44.349
Mary looked puzzled. "What's it for?"

21
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.745
"Just watch me."

22
00:01:46.746 --> 00:01:53.936
Martha ran to the next room and, taking a handle in each hand, began to skip and skip.

23
00:01:53.937 --> 00:01:55.852
She counted up to a hundred.

24
00:01:55.853 --> 00:02:00.871
"I used to be able to skip to five hundred, but I'm out of practice."

25
00:02:00.872 --> 00:02:04.051
"Do you think I could ever skip like that?"

26
00:02:04.052 --> 00:02:08.805
"You just try," urged Martha, handing her the rope.

27
00:02:08.806 --> 00:02:14.678
"You can't skip to a hundred at first, but Mother says nothing will do you more good.

28
00:02:14.679 --> 00:02:18.218
You'll soon build up strength in your arms and legs."

29
00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:20.570
Mary tried skipping rope.

30
00:02:20.571 --> 00:02:26.957
She was not very good at it, but she liked it so much that she did not want to stop.

31
00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:31.168
"Put on your things and skip outdoors," said Martha.

32
00:02:31.169 --> 00:02:33.323
Mary put on her coat and hat.

33
00:02:33.324 --> 00:02:37.093
She opened the door to go out and then turned back.

34
00:02:37.094 --> 00:02:44.857
"Martha," she said slowly, "those were your wages that your mother used to buy this skipping rope. Thank you."

35
00:02:44.858 --> 00:02:47.633
She held out her hand.

36
00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:52.894
Martha laughed and shook her hand. "Now run outside and play."

37
00:02:52.895 --> 00:02:57.902
Mary skipped around the fountain and up one path and down another.

38
00:02:57.903 --> 00:03:04.996
She skipped into the kitchen garden and saw Ben Weatherstaff digging and talking to his robin.

39
00:03:04.997 --> 00:03:10.202
"Well!" he exclaimed. "You've skipped the roses into your cheeks.

40
00:03:10.203 --> 00:03:12.709
I wouldn't have believed that you could do it."

41
00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.680
"I never skipped before. I can only go up to twenty."

42
00:03:16.681 --> 00:03:21.177
"Keep going. You're doing fine." Ben nodded in approval.

43
00:03:21.178 --> 00:03:25.349
"Just see how the robin's watching you. He followed after you yesterday.

44
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.007
He'll be at it again today."

45
00:03:28.008 --> 00:03:33.752
Mary skipped around all the gardens and the orchard, resting every few minutes.

46
00:03:33.753 --> 00:03:39.017
At last she made up her mind to try to skip the length of her favorite path.

47
00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:43.420
She counted up to thirty before she had to stop and rest.

48
00:03:43.421 --> 00:03:49.134
Suddenly she spotted the robin swaying on a long branch of ivy.

49
00:03:49.135 --> 00:03:53.242
"You showed me where the key was yesterday," she said.

50
00:03:53.243 --> 00:03:57.984
"You ought to show me the door today, but I don't believe you know where it is."

51
00:03:57.985 --> 00:04:01.872
The robin flew from the ivy to the top of the wall.

52
00:04:01.873 --> 00:04:05.853
He opened his beak and sang a loud, lovely trill.

53
00:04:05.854 --> 00:04:08.372
Mary laughed with delight.

54
00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:14.293
She stepped closer to him, and what happened next seemed like magic.

55
00:04:14.294 --> 00:04:18.974
A gust of wind swung aside some loose ivy trails.

56
00:04:18.975 --> 00:04:23.035
Mary jumped forward and caught the ivy in her hand.

57
00:04:23.036 --> 00:04:27.995
She'd seen something under the ivy—a round doorknob.

58
00:04:27.996 --> 00:04:31.030
She began to push the leaves aside.

59
00:04:31.031 --> 00:04:36.599
The ivy was thick, but nearly all of it hung in a loose, swinging curtain.

60
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:42.595
Mary's heart thumped, and her hands shook with excitement as she touched the door.

61
00:04:42.596 --> 00:04:45.849
Mary reached into her pocket for the key.

62
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:48.957
She put the key in the lock and turned it.

63
00:04:48.958 --> 00:04:54.939
And then she took a breath and looked up the long path to see if anyone was coming.

64
00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:05.198
No one was there. She took another breath and slowly opened the door.

